1
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,040
Old Sang.

2
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,080
Have you had enough fun yet?

3
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,280
Isn't it time to come back?

4
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,600
If you don't come back soon,

5
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,560
you're gonna work me to death.

6
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,240
Let me tell you,

7
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,240
you'll just have to get used to it.

8
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,760
Until the new battalion commander arrives,

9
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,240
you'll have to hold the fort.

10
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,000
So you're just washing your hands of it?

11
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:09,800
Guo Zijian, let me tell you,

12
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,560
these soldiers of yours

13
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:13,040
are all right here waiting for you.

14
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,840
If you don't come back,

15
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,040
how can you face them?

16
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,400
How is everyone lately?

17
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,440
They haven't slacked on training, right?

18
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,680
Don't worry about that.

19
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,600
They're all acting like men possessed.

20
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,560
Training to death. I couldn't stop them if I tried.

21
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,080
They say

22
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:34,360
only by making the 1st Battalion truly stand tall,

23
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,240
can they naturally keep you here.

24
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:48,840
What's wrong?

25
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:50,520
Touched?

26
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,400
Crying?

27
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,680
Tearing up?

28
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,080
Screw you.

29
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,320
As long as everyone's okay, I'm relieved.

30
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:03,960
Alright.

31
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,200
You should get some sleep too.

32
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:07,120
Stop staying up late, or you'll go bald.

33
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:13,560
Guo Zijian.

34
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,520
Let me tell you something.

35
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,080
If I ever do go bald one day,

36
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,400
it'll absolutely be from worrying about you.

37
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:20,080
You'll have to take responsibility.

38
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,520
Fall in!

39
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:37,080
Hello, old comrades.

40
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,680
Hello, Battalion Commander!

41
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:39,640
Salute!

42
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,120
Comrades,

43
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,960
it's been over thirty years.

44
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:51,760
Today,

45
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,240
we, 1st Battalion, 602nd Regiment, 198th Division,

46
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,280
have reassembled here.

47
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,040
I am very glad.

48
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,560
As your battalion commander,

49
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,800
I welcome you.

50
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:15,600
Setting up this memorial

51
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,360
took a lot of hard work.

52
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,959
We've collected some relics

53
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:20,560
from our time on the frontlines.

54
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,519
Come.

55
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,240
Battalion Commander.

56
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:24,640
Isn't that Old Liu drinking water?

57
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:26,360
Right?

58
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,840
During that forced march,

59
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,880
we only had one canteen for three days.

60
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:32,640
Our throats were burning from thirst.

61
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,480
Old Liu,

62
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,080
you used to be the fastest runner in our battalion.

63
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,040
Look at you.

64
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,360
You've put on so much weight.

65
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,360
Can you still run?

66
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:44,280
I put on weight because my wife is a great cook.

67
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,720
As for whether I can run,

68
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:47,920
want to race me?

69
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:50,400
I won't race you on foot.

70
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:51,320
If we're competing,

71
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,520
let's see who's the better shot.

72
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,160
A shooting contest?

73
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:56,840
This is Old Wang.

74
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,760
Wang Zhaokun, right?

75
00:04:59,040 --> 00:04:59,800
Yes.

76
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:00,960
Yes.

77
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:03,360
In the battle at Height 410,

78
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,840
his arm was injured by a howitzer.

79
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:07,600
When someone took a picture of him,

80
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,080
he insisted on showing his arm.

81
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:11,320
He said it was his medal.

82
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,200
What a show-off.

83
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,760
Anyone who's been on the battlefield

84
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,520
leaves with a few scars.

85
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,080
Yeah, yeah.

86
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:18,920
Where's Old Wang?

87
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:20,240
Why isn't he here?

88
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,880
He got sick last year.

89
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,040
He passed away.

90
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:25,640
Passed away?

91
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:26,800
He wasn't that old.

92
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,640
That's such a shame.

93
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,600
Let's not be too sad.

94
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:34,200
We've all faced life and death.

95
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:37,760
Compared to our comrades who died in battle,

96
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,120
we're still alive.

97
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,280
We're the lucky ones.

98
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,600
You can say that again.

99
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,960
If Old Wang saw us like this,

100
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,040
he'd laugh his head off.

101
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:46,800
That's right.

102
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,960
No matter how many of us are left,

103
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:52,000
we're still the renowned Lightning Battalion.

104
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,320
Right.

105
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,080
Exactly.

106
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:54,560
Right.

107
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,680
Let's keep looking.

108
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:57,680
Okay.

109
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:58,680
Okay.

110
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:00,760
Look.

111
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:02,640
This is

112
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,560
a recoilless rifle.

113
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:04,800
Okay.

114
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:26,800
Reporting!

115
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:28,480
Come in.

116
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,360
Sir.

117
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,320
You wanted to see me?

118
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,440
When people get older,

119
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:40,040
do they tend to reminisce about the past?

120
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,520
I disagree.

121
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,040
First of all,

122
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,200
you're not old, sir.

123
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,400
And,

124
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,880
I think

125
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,680
reminiscing is an acknowledgment of our heritage.

126
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:51,600
Forgetting is the real betrayal, isn't it?

127
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:54,880
Back then, so many of our comrades

128
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:56,040
were buried in foreign lands.

129
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:59,120
This has always weighed heavily on my mind.

130
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,320
You know?

131
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:05,440
Our current troops

132
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,960
haven't experienced war.

133
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:10,040
I'm really afraid they don't know

134
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:12,280
the true cruelty of war.

135
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,400
Peace is hard-won.

136
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,000
But to protect that peace,

137
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,640
we must have troops capable of fighting tough battles,

138
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,560
and formidable military strength backing us up.

139
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:27,920
Otherwise,

140
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:29,800
defending our country

141
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,560
is just empty talk.

142
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,160
You're right, sir.

143
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,240
Is that why

144
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,800
you value Guo Zijian so much?

145
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,760
That's just one reason.

146
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:41,000
He also has certain traits

147
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,280
that always remind me of my old commander.

148
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,320
Back then, I was still a recruit,

149
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:51,360
and went straight to the front lines after enlisting.

150
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,440
That was truly a life-and-death battle.

151
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:03,880
Reporting, Battalion Commander!

152
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:04,920
Go ahead.

153
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,880
Third Company reports.

154
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,120
The breach at Height 410

155
00:08:07,120 --> 00:08:07,840
has been sealed off.

156
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,720
Excellent!

157
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,560
That pork stew didn't go to waste.

158
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,600
They ran fast enough.

159
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,280
This is Chen Hanxiao.

160
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,000
First Company!

161
00:08:19,280 --> 00:08:19,920
First Company here.

162
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:22,120
Third Company has successfully deployed.

163
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,000
In three minutes,

164
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,680
First Company will launch a frontal assault.

165
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:25,560
Yes, sir!

166
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,000
Machine Gun Company, Howitzer Company,

167
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,800
reinforce firepower in First Company's direction.

168
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,720
Saturation strike!

169
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:32,720
Fire!

170
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,360
We were supposed to encircle the enemy.

171
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:41,000
After Third Company engaged,

172
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,360
they suddenly spotted enemy reinforcements

173
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:44,200
arriving from the rear flank,

174
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,800
trying to help the trapped troops break out.

175
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,480
At that time,

176
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:50,640
the old battalion commander

177
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,640
personally led the reserves into battle.

178
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:55,040
I was right beside him.

179
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,560
Battalion Commander!

180
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:20,760
Battalion Commander!

181
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,880
What are you yelling for?

182
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:25,680
I'm not dead yet.

183
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:27,640
Battalion Commander,

184
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,080
this battle is a mess.

185
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:31,960
The enemy reinforced way too fast.

186
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:32,600
The worst part is,

187
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:33,600
they have heavy equipment.

188
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,400
We've lost our window.

189
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,720
Disengage immediately!

190
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:38,840
If we keep fighting like this,

191
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,560
we'll be completely surrounded!

192
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:41,240
Battalion Commander,

193
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,280
pulling out like this

194
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,240
really leaves a bad taste.

195
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,880
We can't fight a losing battle.

196
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:47,720
Follow orders!

197
00:09:47,840 --> 00:09:48,280
Fall back!

198
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,040
Yes, sir!

199
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,280
Fall back!

200
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,640
Fall back! Fall back!

201
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,200
In that battle,

202
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:56,000
we encountered the enemy unexpectedly.

203
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:57,280
I promptly

204
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:59,280
reported to my superiors.

205
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:01,520
But there wasn't much time to react.

206
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:02,800
Headquarters

207
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:05,120
couldn't provide any support either.

208
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,680
If I didn't act, I'd miss the opportunity.

209
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,240
Back then,

210
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,360
I was young,

211
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,760
young and arrogant.

212
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,480
I wanted to make a name for myself,

213
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:15,360
to earn merits.

214
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:17,360
Those were my selfish motives.

215
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,280
That battle

216
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:19,800
was fought too hastily.

217
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,880
Our plans were leaked,

218
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:25,600
costing many comrades their lives.

219
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,640
I failed them.

220
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:30,960
Battalion Commander,

221
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,800
don't blame yourself.

222
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,080
For that battle,

223
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:36,120
I was a direct witness.

224
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,160
We killed over a hundred enemies.

225
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,880
It was considered a major victory.

226
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:41,000
Besides,

227
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:43,440
Headquarters already reached a final conclusion.

228
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:46,040
As for

229
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:47,160
any regrets,

230
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:48,520
after all these years,

231
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:50,560
I think the biggest regret

232
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:52,000
is that our infantry battalion

233
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,880
had such limited firepower.

234
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,200
Right.

235
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,040
We lacked coordination with other branches.

236
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:56,880
Yeah.

237
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,480
The Third Company Commander is right.

238
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,600
The fighting back then

239
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,920
was total chaos.

240
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,160
The enemy was so close to us,

241
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:05,400
we didn't even dare to call in artillery.

242
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,640
Otherwise,

243
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:08,520
one strike would've wiped us all out.

244
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:13,840
Battalion Commander Guo,

245
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:17,120
you are an active-duty

246
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,280
battalion commander in the PLA.

247
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,920
What are your thoughts on this battle?

248
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,960
Listening to everyone just now,

249
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,360
I think

250
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:34,440
the biggest regret of Height 410's battle

251
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:37,200
was that the infantry had no heavy weapons.

252
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,640
After spotting the enemy,

253
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,560
they could only rely on their legs to move.

254
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,840
By the time they arrived,

255
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:44,760
they had already missed the best opportunity.

256
00:11:45,280 --> 00:11:46,920
So when the 3rd Company flanked around

257
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,040
and got into position,

258
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,880
the enemy's reinforcements had also arrived.

259
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:52,400
If it had been today's Combined Arms Battalion,

260
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:53,640
coming with

261
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,440
ground forces firepower

262
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,160
and attached armored vehicles,

263
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:58,880
then that battle

264
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,480
would have been a solid envelopment.

265
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,000
Right.

266
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:01,400
Exactly.

267
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:08,040
In that era, they did nothing wrong.

268
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,120
But now,

269
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:11,080
moving towards combined arms

270
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,200
and focusing on new types of forces,

271
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:13,880
isn't it all so we can adapt

272
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:15,240
to the challenges of modern warfare?

273
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,000
Yeah.

274
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:19,000
But our old battalion commander couldn't get past it.

275
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:20,720
The moment the battle ended,

276
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,840
he started studying battalion tactics.

277
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,560
I think it was the following year,

278
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:26,360
right before I left for the military academy.

279
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:28,160
He came running over excitedly,

280
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,560
holding a large stack of

281
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:31,360
his research findings to me and said,

282
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:32,560
Beihua,

283
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,960
I think that old saying is right.

284
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,240
Changes in equipment and firepower

285
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,600
are what determine

286
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,960
the fundamentals of battlefield tactics.

287
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:47,280
What happened after that?

288
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,440
Did you ever see him again?

289
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:52,200
Not long after,

290
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,000
he applied to be transferred to civilian work.

291
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,240
Before his transfer, he sent me a letter.

292
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,000
The letter said

293
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:01,520
from theories to concepts,

294
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:04,080
and from knowledge to technology,

295
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,560
it was too hard for him to grasp.

296
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:10,360
He hoped I could fulfill his dream.

297
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,120
Since then,

298
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,920
we lost touch.

299
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:18,640
This old battalion commander

300
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:19,760
knew right from wrong

301
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,040
and when to advance and retreat.

302
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:22,720
That's rare.

303
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,040
Yeah.

304
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:34,400
So,

305
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,520
whenever I feel like slacking off,

306
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:39,040
I always think of our old battalion commander.

307
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:41,080
Those eyes full of expectation

308
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:43,720
seem to always be watching me from behind,

309
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:45,240
telling me,

310
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,600
Beihua,

311
00:13:47,920 --> 00:13:49,480
you can't step back.

312
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,120
I know

313
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:53,920
no matter what,

314
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:56,240
I must never step back.

315
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,040
They're here.

316
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:03,280
Quick, quick, quick.

317
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,400
How much did you drink?

318
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:09,600
Once he saw his old comrades today,

319
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,040
he just couldn't hold back.

320
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:14,920
They are my brothers in life and death.

321
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,720
Even if I drink for three days and three nights,

322
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,920
I wouldn't get drunk.

323
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,120
Look how old you are,

324
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:21,400
still talking about drinking for three days and nights.

325
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:22,880
Fangmei,

326
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:24,080
let me tell you.

327
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,640
You are absolutely right.

328
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,560
That kid Zijian is just stubborn.

329
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:30,520
Alright, alright.

330
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,320
Sit down quickly.

331
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:33,800
I'll go pour you a glass of honey water.

332
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,640
Let me tell you.

333
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:40,200
He is my flesh and blood.

334
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:42,720
In his body,

335
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,800
the blood of a soldier flows.

336
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,160
You have no idea.

337
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,320
Today,

338
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:50,360
the moment he stood in front of the sand table,

339
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,600
his eyes lit up.

340
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,280
I knew right then.

341
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:55,920
I figured out what was on his mind

342
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,120
just by testing him a little.

343
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:06,600
Fangmei,

344
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:07,840
your phone.

345
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:10,840
Could you answer it for me and ask who it is?

346
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:17,240
Director Qi.

347
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,440
I asked around.

348
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:20,840
I heard your Zijian got disciplined.

349
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,360
Apparently, during the exercise,

350
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,640
he made some kind of mistake.

351
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:24,440
Afterward, he refused to accept it

352
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:26,000
and made a scene at the Party committee.

353
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,360
I don't know the exact details.

354
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:30,760
That's impossible.

355
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,040
Where are you going?

356
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,960
What's gotten into my dad?

357
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:39,720
I don't know.

358
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,680
Quick, go after him!

359
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:41,760
Go, go, go!

360
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:55,320
Grandma.

361
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,480
Why isn't Grandpa sleeping inside?

362
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,600
Why are you just getting back?

363
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,320
He waited for you all night and wouldn't sleep.

364
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:03,480
Well, he

365
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:05,680
insisted on hearing you talk

366
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,800
about that old comrades' reunion.

367
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:09,400
He just fell asleep.

368
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,280
Let's get him inside to sleep.

369
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,200
Old Chen, calm down.

370
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:16,880
Dad, Dad!

371
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,240
Go, quickly!

372
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:19,880
Guo Zijian!

373
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:24,160
Tell me the truth.

374
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,920
Were you kicked out of the army?

375
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:26,560
Dad.

376
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,680
Let's talk this out calmly.

377
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:28,960
I can't talk calmly!

378
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:29,880
Let me tell you,

379
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:32,200
I've been in the army for so many years,

380
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,800
and I've always walked a straight line.

381
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,800
I've never done anything to violate discipline!

382
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:36,920
But you,

383
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,520
you dare to make a scene at the committee!

384
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:39,720
Tell me,

385
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:41,360
what the hell did you do?

386
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:42,080
Old Chen,

387
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:43,880
this isn't set in stone yet, is it?

388
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,320
It might not be the kid's fault.

389
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:46,920
If it's not his fault, whose is it?

390
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:48,080
Don't try to defend him here.

391
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,120
The army

392
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:50,880
won't wrong a good person.

393
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:51,880
Let me tell you,

394
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,120
if you were my soldier,

395
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,480
I'd shoot you dead!

396
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,840
Then just shoot me!

397
00:16:57,760 --> 00:16:58,280
Dad!

398
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:01,040
Dad, how could you hit him?

399
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:01,920
Hanxiao!

400
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:02,560
Dad!

401
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:03,680
Brother!

402
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:10,920
Brother!

403
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:13,079
Look at what you did.

404
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:18,319
Old man! Old man!

405
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,079
Honestly,

406
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:23,520
you went too far in front of the old man.

407
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:26,079
The kid knows he made a mistake,

408
00:17:26,079 --> 00:17:27,280
which is why he came home.

409
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,960
He's definitely hurting inside too.

410
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,840
With that slap of yours,

411
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:32,840
you really broke his heart.

412
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:52,440
Mom.

413
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:56,320
He was never proud of me.

414
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,000
And now I'm his disgrace.

415
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:09,160
Are you disappointed in me, too?

416
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,600
Be good at home.

417
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:19,000
I'm scared.

418
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:20,880
Dad's in a hurry.

419
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,920
Mom will be right back, okay?

420
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:23,680
No.

421
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:28,800
Sweetie.

422
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:31,480
You're the bravest little soldier.

423
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:32,640
Didn't you say

424
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,680
you love Mom's shredded pork noodles the most?

425
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:35,720
Yeah.

426
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:37,720
Then go finish them.

427
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:38,840
Once you finish your noodles,

428
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:39,840
Mom will be back.

429
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Promise?

430
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,840
Promise.

431
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,440
Remember to hurry back.

432
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:46,440
Bye.

433
00:18:47,520 --> 00:18:48,240
Wait for Mom.

434
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,280
Where's Mom?

435
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,200
Why isn't Mom back?

436
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,160
"Mom will be back soon."

437
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,880
She told me so.

438
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:35,760
Once I finish these hot pork noodles,

439
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:37,080
she'll be back.

440
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,840
Why hasn't she come back yet?

441
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,320
Dad.

442
00:20:42,520 --> 00:20:44,400
Please take me to find Mom.

443
00:20:48,320 --> 00:20:50,360
Please take me to find Mom.

444
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:54,120
I want Mom to come back.

445
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:55,160
Dad.

446
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,480
I want Mom.

447
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,680
I want Mom to come back.

448
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,520
Dad.

449
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:00,880
I want Mom.

450
00:21:00,880 --> 00:21:02,960
I want Mom to come back.

451
00:21:02,960 --> 00:21:05,600
Dad, I want Mom.

452
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:19,920
Mom.

453
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,200
I miss you.

454
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:32,400
I'm craving your shredded pork noodles.

455
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,600
Guo Zijian's reflection on the exercise.

456
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:44,560
I've read it.

457
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:47,200
I think this article

458
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:49,920
mainly reflects on the exercise's issues,

459
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,680
like prioritizing rules and scores,

460
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,320
outdated tactics,

461
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:55,200
and one-dimensional directing methods.

462
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,280
Since

463
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:57,800
it is based on actual practice,

464
00:21:57,880 --> 00:22:00,080
some of his data is quite accurate

465
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:00,840
and highly valuable.

466
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:04,080
Especially some of his suggestions,

467
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:05,360
which are quite brilliant.

468
00:22:06,120 --> 00:22:06,880
However,

469
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:08,960
I think he wrote this article

470
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,640
on the day the evaluation ended.

471
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:12,720
It's very emotional

472
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,120
and highly subjective.

473
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,960
You put it very objectively.

474
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:18,640
I'm basically satisfied.

475
00:22:18,760 --> 00:22:19,760
So I pass.

476
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:22,600
Sir,

477
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:24,000
I was thinking,

478
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,440
why not take this article

479
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:28,080
and, in the name of the Group Army Staff,

480
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,080
forward it to the troops.

481
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:31,280
Let everyone study and analyze it together.

482
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:33,880
This would also be highly beneficial

483
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:35,040
for future exercises and training.

484
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,040
Forward the original text?

485
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:36,840
Yes.

486
00:22:37,160 --> 00:22:38,160
Everyone will have different views.

487
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,040
Let them judge for themselves.

488
00:22:40,920 --> 00:22:42,680
I agree with forwarding the original text,

489
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:43,960
but not right now.

490
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:44,880
Why?

491
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:45,840
Think about it.

492
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:47,040
The disciplinary decision on Guo Zijian

493
00:22:47,040 --> 00:22:48,200
hasn't been finalized yet.

494
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:50,120
If we forward his article

495
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:52,400
reflecting on the exercise right now,

496
00:22:52,680 --> 00:22:54,600
wouldn't that obviously be clearing his name?

497
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:56,760
Can we do something like that?

498
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:59,000
I didn't think it through.

499
00:22:59,800 --> 00:23:00,360
However,

500
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:02,360
speaking of handling Guo Zijian,

501
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:03,840
I think Kang Baoping

502
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,720
is quite interesting.

503
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:06,000
You noticed it too.

504
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:07,920
Let me tell you,

505
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,240
Kang Baoping

506
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:12,200
put Guo Zijian on leave...

507
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:13,160
First,

508
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:15,800
it's to let Guo Zijian calm down.

509
00:23:16,080 --> 00:23:16,960
Second,

510
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,760
it's to protect Guo Zijian.

511
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:19,800
Third,

512
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:22,400
it gives the Party committee a buffer.

513
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,360
Very wise.

514
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,320
Old Kang

515
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,800
is truly a veteran political officer.

516
00:23:28,480 --> 00:23:29,960
Guo Zijian has a distinct personality

517
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:31,000
and dares to take responsibility,

518
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:32,200
but he still lacks maturity.

519
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:33,040
If things go wrong,

520
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,040
after a few stumbles,

521
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,640
he could turn into a meek sheep

522
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,600
and be completely ruined.

523
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,440
There is another possibility.

524
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:41,320
After a few ups and downs,

525
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,080
he becomes a moth drawn to a flame.

526
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:45,320
Therefore,

527
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,720
an officer's growth,

528
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:49,360
besides being tempered,

529
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:52,200
also relies on the organization's care.

530
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:57,000
When you have time,

531
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,520
learn more from Kang Baoping.

532
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,320
Rest assured, sir.

533
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:32,520
Pour.

534
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:57,320
We've had our drinks.

535
00:24:58,760 --> 00:24:59,960
Ask whatever you want to ask.

536
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,760
I'm not asking today.

537
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:03,280
You tell me yourself.

538
00:25:04,040 --> 00:25:04,920
Tell you what?

539
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,640
That my thoughts,

540
00:25:08,080 --> 00:25:09,120
my actions,

541
00:25:09,560 --> 00:25:10,920
or even my existence,

542
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,160
are not understood,

543
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:13,120
and not accepted?

544
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:16,200
Just because I want to be a soldier

545
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,320
always ready, daring to fight and win,

546
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:21,280
does that make me a destabilizing factor in the unit?

547
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:23,680
Just like they said,

548
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:25,560
if I stay in the army,

549
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:27,440
I'd probably be a menace.

550
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,200
So you went and made a scene at the base?

551
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:31,680
I did make a scene,

552
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:34,360
but it wasn't for myself.

553
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:36,480
I was requesting a merit citation

554
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:38,800
for the comrade who lost his right leg

555
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:40,520
That's the honor he deserves.

556
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:43,040
A soldier's duty is to follow orders.

557
00:25:43,440 --> 00:25:44,720
As a soldier,

558
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,000
you must be ready to sacrifice at any time.

559
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:53,400
I just feel that

560
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:57,840
Wu Dongsheng is the best scout.

561
00:25:58,840 --> 00:25:59,840
He is an Ace Soldier.

562
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:03,280
After his amputation, he has to go home.

563
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,840
His whole life has completely changed.

564
00:26:08,320 --> 00:26:10,600
Why couldn't they give him a merit citation?

565
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:12,960
The injury to his leg

566
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:13,800
is directly

567
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:15,320
related to you, isn't it?

568
00:26:17,520 --> 00:26:19,440
So you went to your superiors to make a scene.

569
00:26:19,640 --> 00:26:21,480
You feel that you owe him.

570
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:23,400
Your anger and dissatisfaction

571
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:25,120
are just to cover up

572
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:26,880
your guilt towards him.

573
00:26:26,880 --> 00:26:27,320
Right?

574
00:26:30,360 --> 00:26:31,000
Son,

575
00:26:31,920 --> 00:26:33,520
it's okay to make mistakes.

576
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:37,480
But you must face them properly.

577
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:43,600
It's been over twenty years.

578
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,400
The two of us

579
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:48,280
have never sat down for a real talk.

580
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:49,560
I know you hate me.

581
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:51,640
I do hate you.

582
00:26:54,360 --> 00:26:55,800
It was raining so heavily then.

583
00:26:57,120 --> 00:26:57,760
Why did you

584
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:59,600
insist my mom deliver those documents to you?

585
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:03,040
Was your project really that important?

586
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:05,280
More important than my mom's life?

587
00:27:07,280 --> 00:27:08,440
I really wish...

588
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:09,600
You wish

589
00:27:10,520 --> 00:27:12,320
the one who died then wasn't your mom,

590
00:27:12,320 --> 00:27:12,920
but me.

591
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:16,360
I've thought about that too.

592
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:18,000
I wished that I had died

593
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,240
instead of your mother.

594
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:21,760
I'd be willing to give up everything

595
00:27:23,760 --> 00:27:25,520
to bring your mother back to life.

596
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:32,000
Right before your mother died,

597
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:33,640
she told me

598
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,640
to take good care of you.

599
00:27:37,320 --> 00:27:39,400
And then you dumped me at my grandparents'?

600
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:42,080
For the college entrance exam,

601
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:44,040
you secretly changed my applications.

602
00:27:44,320 --> 00:27:45,680
Is that how you take care of me?

603
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,560
After your mother passed away,

604
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:49,440
I was devastated.

605
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:50,640
Deep in my heart,

606
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:52,520
I couldn't get over it for years.

607
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:54,960
I didn't know how to face you.

608
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,640
So I just buried

609
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:58,040
myself in work.

610
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:00,240
Over the years,

611
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:03,120
we drifted further and further apart.

612
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:05,960
Later, I got together with your Aunt Qi.

613
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:07,160
I thought things would be fine then.

614
00:28:07,160 --> 00:28:08,520
Someone would be there to take care of you.

615
00:28:08,920 --> 00:28:09,840
I didn't expect

616
00:28:11,240 --> 00:28:12,920
that once you went to your grandpa's,

617
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:14,320
you would never come back.

618
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:15,960
Stop talking.

619
00:28:16,040 --> 00:28:16,520
No.

620
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,080
Since we're talking about it today,

621
00:28:18,240 --> 00:28:19,560
I'm going to make things clear.

622
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,040
I know

623
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:23,040
I am a very authoritarian person.

624
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:24,120
Back then,

625
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:26,360
when you graduated from high school,

626
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:27,840
you actually wanted to apply

627
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:29,120
to a military academy.

628
00:28:29,320 --> 00:28:31,560
But you just had to defy me

629
00:28:31,560 --> 00:28:33,160
and insist on a civilian university.

630
00:28:34,440 --> 00:28:36,040
I didn't even know how to reason with you.

631
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:38,880
All these years,

632
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:40,360
you wouldn't even

633
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:41,480
answer my calls,

634
00:28:44,880 --> 00:28:46,680
or call me Dad.

635
00:28:50,040 --> 00:28:51,640
As a father, I have been

636
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:53,120
an absolute failure.

637
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:01,400
Actually, I know

638
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:06,120
what happened to my mom wasn't your fault,

639
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:10,160
but I don't know who to blame.

640
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:15,720
If I had been

641
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:18,640
a little more mature

642
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:21,480
and a little braver,

643
00:29:23,760 --> 00:29:25,960
my mom wouldn't have been rushing so much,

644
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:29,040
and the accident wouldn't have happened.

645
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:30,680
This isn't your fault.

646
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:32,880
It's not.

647
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:36,280
There are no "ifs" in life.

648
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:39,600
You have to be brave enough to face reality.

649
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:41,680
Right now,

650
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:44,600
you've hit a hurdle in your life.

651
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:46,600
I hope you can face it.

652
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:50,680
I believe the army will give you this chance.

653
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:54,280
Maybe I'm really not suited to stay in the army.

654
00:29:55,920 --> 00:29:58,080
At least not in the 396th Brigade.

655
00:29:58,160 --> 00:29:58,680
No.

656
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:00,920
There is no one

657
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:02,640
more suited for the army than you.

658
00:30:02,720 --> 00:30:04,760
Or more suited to be a soldier.

659
00:30:05,120 --> 00:30:07,640
But how to become a real soldier...

660
00:30:07,720 --> 00:30:09,200
That is up to you.

661
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:11,720
I grew up listening to

662
00:30:13,080 --> 00:30:14,800
Grandpa's war stories.

663
00:30:16,880 --> 00:30:18,440
I saw you in your uniform

664
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:20,360
as my idol.

665
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:23,680
Even though our conflicts once

666
00:30:24,120 --> 00:30:25,160
make me not want to be a soldier,

667
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:28,680
from the moment I put on this uniform,

668
00:30:29,280 --> 00:30:30,160
I knew

669
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:32,440
this was my calling.

670
00:30:34,840 --> 00:30:35,960
If I'm not in the army,

671
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:36,720
if I'm not a soldier,

672
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:39,680
I really don't know what else suits me.

673
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:44,000
But right now,

674
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:46,760
it's too hard.

675
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:50,320
I feel like I just

676
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,320
don't fit in with everyone.

677
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:53,960
Are you going to give up?

678
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:56,280
As a soldier,

679
00:30:56,920 --> 00:30:58,960
if you fail to capture a position,

680
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:00,400
do you choose to retreat,

681
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:02,400
or take a detour?

682
00:31:03,960 --> 00:31:06,040
I used to be very arbitrary with you,

683
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:07,400
but today,

684
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:09,120
I respect your choice.

685
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:12,840
If you choose to escape or leave,

686
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:17,760
for the rest of your life,

687
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:20,000
won't you regret it?

688
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:22,280
Won't you feel remorse?

689
00:31:37,240 --> 00:31:37,880
Grandma.

690
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:42,240
Zijian, your grandpa is missing.

691
00:32:25,480 --> 00:32:29,200
Cmdr., 2nd Bn, 178th Reg, 60th Div,

692
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:30,360
Guo Yougen,

693
00:32:30,360 --> 00:32:31,400
reporting for duty.

694
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:55,800
I am Guo Zijian.

695
00:32:58,840 --> 00:32:59,880
Yijiangshan Island

696
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:11,160
Guo Zijian.

697
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:15,240
Why are you here?

698
00:33:15,600 --> 00:33:16,720
I was at the police station on business,

699
00:33:17,040 --> 00:33:18,360
and I happened to hear your name.

700
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:19,520
I saw the photo, and it really was you.

701
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:21,760
So I volunteered to take the job,

702
00:33:21,760 --> 00:33:23,080
to repay you for saving my life.

703
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:24,280
Thank you.

704
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:26,360
Don't worry.

705
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:27,360
Your grandfather is fine.

706
00:33:27,840 --> 00:33:29,280
The unit has taken good care of him.

707
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:30,360
They even arranged for a doctor

708
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:31,680
to give him a full medical checkup.

709
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:33,000
Okay, let's hurry over.

710
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:36,040
Thanks, Commissar, for caring for Grandpa.

711
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:36,960
Battalion Commander Guo,

712
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:38,280
don't mention it.

713
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:40,720
Veteran Guo is a hero of our brigade.

714
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,360
We normally couldn't get him here even if we tried.

715
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:45,000
If he wasn't always thinking of his unit,

716
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:46,400
he wouldn't constantly

717
00:33:46,400 --> 00:33:47,480
be thinking about coming back.

718
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:48,600
However,

719
00:33:48,600 --> 00:33:49,760
looking at his current condition,

720
00:33:49,760 --> 00:33:51,720
it seems there's a problem with his memory.

721
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,240
Our medical officer examined him.

722
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:54,080
It's nothing major.

723
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:56,200
His condition is basically stable.

724
00:33:56,320 --> 00:33:57,240
Take good care of him at home,

725
00:33:57,280 --> 00:33:58,840
and find a hospital to run more tests.

726
00:33:59,040 --> 00:33:59,600
I will.

727
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:01,440
Grandpa.

728
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:03,040
I'm not going back with him.

729
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:07,400
My grandson is in the PLA.

730
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:09,120
An active-duty Army major.

731
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,199
A battalion commander.

732
00:34:11,199 --> 00:34:12,199
Who are you?

733
00:34:16,040 --> 00:34:16,760
Sir,

734
00:34:17,120 --> 00:34:18,480
he is your grandson.

735
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:19,880
Guo Zijian, Battalion Commander Guo.

736
00:34:20,560 --> 00:34:21,440
I don't know him.

737
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:26,679
Officer's ID.

738
00:34:32,280 --> 00:34:32,840
Grandpa,

739
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:33,560
look.

740
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:37,360
Old Battalion Commander,

741
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:38,880
please check for me.

742
00:34:38,880 --> 00:34:40,159
Is he impersonating an officer?

743
00:34:40,159 --> 00:34:40,840
If he is,

744
00:34:40,960 --> 00:34:42,120
I'll arrest him immediately.

745
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:43,560
I don't know.

746
00:34:45,239 --> 00:34:45,719
Go back.

747
00:34:46,560 --> 00:34:47,280
Grandpa.

748
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:54,800
Battalion Commander Guo,

749
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:55,880
I don't think this will work.

750
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:57,400
Let the old man stay here

751
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:58,520
for a couple more days of observation.

752
00:35:02,120 --> 00:35:02,600
Okay.

753
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:03,520
Thank you, Commissar.

754
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:26,920
Let's go, Squad Leader!

755
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:28,800
Keep going!

756
00:35:33,600 --> 00:35:34,480
Battalion Commander.

757
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:35,760
Did you see that?

758
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:37,440
Even though I'm missing a leg,

759
00:35:37,520 --> 00:35:39,440
I can still live life to the fullest.

760
00:35:39,440 --> 00:35:41,440
And I can still win battles.

761
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:43,520
"Good iron isn't used for nails,"

762
00:35:43,760 --> 00:35:45,320
"but good men must become soldiers."

763
00:35:45,640 --> 00:35:46,600
All these years,

764
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:48,600
I have no regrets.

765
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:50,320
Battalion Commander...

766
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:51,360
But,

767
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:53,040
the journey isn't over yet.

768
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:54,280
This path...

769
00:35:54,560 --> 00:35:56,400
can you keep walking it for me?

770
00:35:59,560 --> 00:36:00,240
Squad Leader Wu.

771
00:36:00,920 --> 00:36:01,720
The car is here.

772
00:36:03,560 --> 00:36:04,280
Battalion Commander,

773
00:36:07,160 --> 00:36:08,080
I'm leaving now.

774
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:10,640
Before I go home,

775
00:36:13,240 --> 00:36:15,360
I want to hear you call the roll one last time.

776
00:36:26,920 --> 00:36:27,800
Wu Dongsheng

777
00:36:28,280 --> 00:36:29,360
Here

778
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:31,600
Wu Dongsheng

779
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:33,800
Here

780
00:36:49,840 --> 00:36:51,000
Wu Dongsheng.

781
00:36:51,520 --> 00:36:55,080
Here!

782
00:37:21,960 --> 00:37:22,720
Alright.

783
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:25,560
Everyone.

784
00:37:26,120 --> 00:37:26,800
Attention!

785
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:29,440
Battalion Commander.

786
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,960
Hurry home.

787
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:35,520
Zijian, come back!

788
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:37,880
Grandpa.

789
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:40,200
The army really didn't discharge me.

790
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:41,920
Everyone's waiting for me to get back.

791
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:44,080
Okay.

792
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:45,560
Let's go home.

793
00:38:06,440 --> 00:38:10,120
Brigade Commander, our battalion commander has already agreed.

794
00:38:18,240 --> 00:38:19,160
Traitor.

795
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,440
Deserter.

796
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:27,400
Yang Maolin.

797
00:38:28,480 --> 00:38:29,880
What do you think the military is?

798
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:32,880
Some brotherhood built on blind loyalty?

799
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:34,880
Bullshit!

800
00:38:35,560 --> 00:38:38,720
The military is a wall of iron discipline.

801
00:38:42,560 --> 00:38:43,800
Why so quiet?

802
00:38:44,840 --> 00:38:47,200
I thought you were quite the talker, Yang Maolin.

803
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:48,520
That transfer report of yours...

804
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:50,120
Wasn't it written with such deep devotion...

805
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:51,040
and sounding so high and mighty?

806
00:38:51,040 --> 00:38:51,720
Group Commander...

807
00:38:52,120 --> 00:38:53,080
No, Brigade Commander.

808
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,480
So you remember I'm your Group Commander.

809
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:58,880
If I had known you'd turn out to be a deserter,

810
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,600
I never should have, back in Special Ops,

811
00:39:00,600 --> 00:39:02,280
fought so hard to recommend you.

812
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:40,960
Maolin.

813
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:44,280
We all make mistakes when we're young.

814
00:39:45,600 --> 00:39:46,680
Considering your youth,

815
00:39:47,040 --> 00:39:48,000
and that it's a first offense,

816
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:50,760
plus you're a soldier I trained myself...

817
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:52,600
I can't exactly take you

818
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:54,080
and ruin your whole career over this, can I?

819
00:39:54,280 --> 00:39:55,240
Commander, I...

820
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:56,360
Enough stammering.

821
00:39:56,960 --> 00:39:58,040
Knowing your mistake is enough.

822
00:39:58,640 --> 00:39:59,360
This time,

823
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:00,680
I'm making a special exception:

824
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:02,160
no self-criticism in front of the brigade.

825
00:40:02,680 --> 00:40:04,680
What kind of place is the 396th Brigade?

826
00:40:04,680 --> 00:40:06,000
It's not like you don't know.

827
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:09,400
If you went there, you'd be jumping right into the fire.

828
00:40:10,280 --> 00:40:10,880
Look at

829
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:12,760
a capable fighter,

830
00:40:12,760 --> 00:40:14,440
someone like Guo Zijian who wants to fight.

831
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:16,360
Even he was worn down and sent packing.

832
00:40:17,080 --> 00:40:18,160
Who do you think you are in comparison?

833
00:40:19,040 --> 00:40:20,400
If you actually went,

834
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:22,440
with your reckless and impulsive attitude,

835
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:23,880
they'd use

836
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:25,840
passive-aggressive tactics against you.

837
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:29,200
Alright.

838
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:30,600
We'll consider this matter

839
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:32,040
closed for now.

840
00:40:33,360 --> 00:40:34,120
Commander...

841
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:38,160
Save the sentimental talk.

842
00:40:38,560 --> 00:40:39,920
Just do your job well

843
00:40:39,920 --> 00:40:41,480
and make up for your mistakes.

844
00:40:42,240 --> 00:40:44,280
The military's various systems

845
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:45,400
are all currently improving.

846
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:47,080
The future for NCOs

847
00:40:47,160 --> 00:40:48,760
is looking very promising.

848
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:49,880
It all depends on what you make of it.

849
00:40:49,880 --> 00:40:50,520
Commander...

850
00:40:50,600 --> 00:40:52,200
You don't need to say anything else.

851
00:40:52,280 --> 00:40:53,560
I know what you're thinking.

852
00:40:54,080 --> 00:40:55,360
You don't need to be grateful to me.

853
00:40:56,160 --> 00:40:57,200
Just work hard,

854
00:40:57,520 --> 00:40:59,200
and fulfill your duties to the fullest.

855
00:40:59,200 --> 00:41:01,800
That's the best way to repay the organization.

856
00:41:03,480 --> 00:41:04,200
Alright.

857
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:05,200
Head back.

858
00:41:05,280 --> 00:41:06,680
I have a lot of work to catch up on.

859
00:41:06,960 --> 00:41:08,440
But Commander, I...

860
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:09,960
Are we done here?

861
00:41:11,160 --> 00:41:12,120
Go back and think about it carefully.

862
00:41:12,120 --> 00:41:13,320
If you still don't get it, go run laps

863
00:41:13,480 --> 00:41:14,880
until you finally do.

864
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:31,040
Stubborn mule.

865
00:41:34,280 --> 00:41:34,880
Staff Officer Liang.

866
00:41:35,240 --> 00:41:36,640
Half hot, half cold.

867
00:41:36,640 --> 00:41:37,040
Warm.

868
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,000
Thank you.

869
00:41:40,680 --> 00:41:41,560
Instructor Sang.

870
00:41:41,560 --> 00:41:44,720
The exercise review for the 396th Brigade

871
00:41:44,720 --> 00:41:45,960
has now been fully completed.

872
00:41:45,960 --> 00:41:47,800
We will return to the base this afternoon.

873
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:49,960
If the comrades have any other questions,

874
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:51,720
feel free to compile and send them to me.

875
00:41:51,720 --> 00:41:53,000
Thank you so much, Staff Officer Liang.

876
00:41:53,560 --> 00:41:56,480
It's the first time a base evaluator

877
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:58,120
has conducted a review for us.

878
00:41:58,200 --> 00:41:58,960
I don't know if you've

879
00:41:59,160 --> 00:42:01,520
checked the Theater Army Frontier Forum.

880
00:42:01,520 --> 00:42:03,560
The troops' positive comments fill screen after screen.

881
00:42:03,560 --> 00:42:04,600
It's practically blowing up.

882
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:07,840
Actually, these grassroots reviews

883
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:09,240
was Commander Ma's idea.

884
00:42:09,240 --> 00:42:11,520
I'm merely doing my duty.

885
00:42:16,160 --> 00:42:16,760
Staff Officer Liang,

886
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:19,800
on behalf of our Battalion Commander,

887
00:42:20,840 --> 00:42:22,000
I really want to thank you.

888
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:25,200
Your Battalion Commander...

889
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:25,840
Actually,

890
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:28,160
I feel deep down that

891
00:42:28,880 --> 00:42:30,160
the situation with our Battalion Commander

892
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:32,960
isn't set in stone yet.

893
00:42:33,720 --> 00:42:34,720
There is still room to turn things around.

894
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:37,440
However,

895
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:39,520
it depends on whether he himself

896
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:41,520
can wrap his head around it.

897
00:42:42,720 --> 00:42:45,320
I've tried talking sense into him every way I can,

898
00:42:46,560 --> 00:42:49,160
and now even I don't know what to do.
